======================================================================
TEST 3: INDEX OF COINCIDENCE (mapping-independent)
======================================================================
IC proves what language and code length the cipher uses
WITHOUT needing a specific mapping.

  1-digit units: IC = 0.108252, normalized = 1.083, alphabet = 10 unique units
  2-digit units: IC = 0.016474, normalized = 1.647, alphabet = 100 unique units
  3-digit units: IC = 0.005347, normalized = 2.411, alphabet = 451 unique units

Interpretation:
  - 2-digit normalized IC near 1.67 = German text (CONFIRMS cipher type)
  - 1-digit or 3-digit IC near 1.67 would mean different code length
  - IC = 1.0 would mean random/no structure

RESULT: PASS - 2-digit IC confirms structured German text

